  "originalPublicScreenLimitations": [
    "12 independent paired processes, six AB and six BA. Within each process case order fixed; calibrated short (~30ms target) measurement is a feasibility screen, not JMH qualification.",
    "Current f360 source baseline and prototype class overlays on retained8d030adb JDK27 x86_64. Identical public-caller harness bytecode; no Vector API. Not a whole-JDK current-master build, not a current PR3/4/5 combined-image result.",
    "Default Names uses StringNameTable, so Names.fromUtf measurements are unaffected controls, not patched Utf8NameTable evidence. Full cold/warmed javac is unmeasured.",
    "No explicit GC; all samples retained. Bootstrap intervals nominal and do not cure JIT/warmup/order uncertainty."
  ],
  "PR3Scope": "DecimalResiduals.java alone is the original decimal model. grouped limits to 9/18 digits with Long.MIN_VALUE collision-free sentinel and original Integer/Long parser fallback. put8 writes exactly eight decimal bytes; no char[] or UTF16 implementation, benchmark or production patch is represented.",
  "PR5Scope": "The f360-only Pattern overlay covers String-backed Slice/BnM paths, with original custom/mutable CharSequence fallback. It is not reconciled with native PR5. Both Slice and BnM store a newly allocated literal String, creating compile allocation cost; +128 B/op for regex_compile_match_32 is retained.",
